# yara-lab local state. Nothing here is source.

# Run artefacts. `out/last-run-yara.json` is a record of ONE run on ONE machine: the
# matched rule names, the observed exit status, the stdout byte count and the scratch
# directory path are all regenerated by tools/probe.mjs and none of them is a property of
# the tree. The root .gitignore already excludes /native-lab/out/, /crypto-lab/out/ and the
# rest of the labs for exactly this reason; this is the same rule applied locally so it does
# not need a second edit to the shared file, which is read-only to this capability's author.
out/

# No .yar file is committed, ever, and this line is the reason that stays true by accident
# only if it is written down. A checked-in rule goes stale against the corpus silently: the
# corpus changes, the rule still compiles, the probe still exits 0, and it is now answering a
# question about a binary that no longer exists. Both tools generate their rules into a
# per-run temp directory and delete them on the way out.
*.yar